    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Alright everyone, settle down. We've all heard the new 'green energy' mandates from down in DC, right? They're talking about revolutionary wind farms and solar grids in the title of the bill, but do you really mean that right now? My friend in Ohio just got the eviction notice because his heating oil tank is empty, not because his roof isn't 'carbon neutral' enough. They're routing billions of that international aid package to 'developing nations' like a free-ride for the Congress party while my neighbor in Pennsylvania can't even afford the grocery store right across the corner.\"\n\"Here's the truth for you: this isn't about ideology anymore; it's about the fact that people can't be made to care about a policy until they feel the consequence in their own back pocket. The people in the White House have a very different time to the people in the rust belt at the very end of the day. They are running a 4:00 a.m. meeting in the Oval office right now, and I just woke up from a 12-hour shift on the factory line because my son needs coverage. Stop pretending that the top people see the same reality I do. I just want to make",
